darkice
------------------------------------------
DarkIce is a live audio streamer. It records audio from an audio interface
(e.g. sound card), encodes it and sends it to a streaming server.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.10-1
  libFLAC14-1.5.0-1
  libfaac0-1.50-1bl1
  libfdk-aac2-2.0.0-2
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libmp3lame0-3.100-1
  libogg0-1.3.6-1
  libopus0-1.6.1-1
  libpulse-simple0-17.0-4
  libpulse0-17.0-4
  libsamplerate0-0.2.2-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libtwolame0-0.4.0-1
  libvorbis0-1.3.7-1
  libvorbisenc2-1.3.7-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-15-3
  automake-20250528-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.7-1
  flac-devel-1.5.0-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libfaac-devel-1.50-1bl1
  libfdk-aac-devel-2.0.0-2
  libmp3lame-devel-3.100-1
  libogg-devel-1.3.6-1
  libopus-devel-1.6.1-1
  libpulse-devel-17.0-4
  libsamplerate-devel-0.2.2-1
  libtwolame-devel-0.4.0-1
  libvorbis-devel-1.3.7-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/rafael2k/darkice

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/rafael2k/darkice/archive/refs/tags/v1.6.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack darkice-1.6-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./darkice-1.6-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/darkice-1.6-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/darkice-1.6-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(darkice)
  /etc/darkice.cfg
